<http://data.silknow.org/object/aa6eb82e-9fe1-36ba-9cae-5050e0030c55/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Italian, early 18th century Altar cloth. Fine white linen ground, pieced in several places, embroidered with fine white linen thread in button hole, stem and chain stitches and a variety of openwork stitches. Borders show rows of birds, animals and flowers. A circular medallion in center containing IHS, with cross and three nails, surrounded by a burst of rays and pinks. Narrow scalloped bobbin lace edging all around. A number of small darned places."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/aa6eb82e-9fe1-36ba-9cae-5050e0030c55> .

